message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "CryptoCPU: design and implementation of an encrypted instruction set processor on FPGA"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "George David"
    family-names: "Tsitlauri"
    affiliation: "Department of Informatics and Telecommunications, University of Thessaly, Lamia, Greece"
  - given-names: "George"
    family-names: "Dimitriou"
    affiliation: "Department of Informatics and Telecommunications, University of Thessaly, Lamia, Greece"
date-released: 2026-10-07
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gdtsitlauri/CryptoCPU"
abstract: >-
  A six-stage, in-order MIPS32-subset processor that executes AES-128-encrypted programs. Address-dependent
  AES-XEX protects instruction blocks, an internal cache reuses decrypted instructions, and code, tweak and
  data-operation keys are separate. Built on a 2025 B.Sc. thesis whose prototype ran on an Artix-7 FPGA.
keywords: [encrypted execution, AES-128, XEX, processor pipeline, FPGA, high-level synthesis, hardware security]
